looksByNameT -- looks by name (Tony, 2026-11-20, SEQ 723 R2-R4). firstLight carries looks:=firstLightLooks, a list of two looks,
standard (pageFill wall) and dark (pageFill black); the first is the default. It is drawn to test.pdf with no look, with
look="standard", with look="dark", and with look="print", a name its list lacks: refused by name, nothing laid out: redrawForm says so on stderr and writes no PDF.
Pixel (450,15) is the heading, which has no fill of its own: the page fill, so the look shows there. Pixel (200,580) is inside the
held descriptions form, which has no list: it uses defaultLook silently (R1, no trace); its lightGreen is explicit, so it reads the
same on every page (the control). lbHost (standard wall, dark black) holds lbHeld, whose list has standard only (red): under standard
lbHeld finds the name, no trace; under dark its list lacks it, so it uses its own default, standard, red, and a trace line says so
(ruled 2026-11-20). Pixels (190,10) host page, (190,190) held page. The print page's pixels are the dark
page's PDF, unwritten: the row reads redrawForm's line, never the pixels.
The spelling is look="dark", by name: a list member is on no search list, so look:=dark is refused at define (measured SEQ 723).
